cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic Optical/Near-IR Echelle & Radio Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and instrumental provenance
  audits for panchromatic optical and near-infrared laser technosignatures (0.38-1.80 um
  across ESO HARPS, VLT ESPRESSO, ESO NIRPS, and FEROS; 80 unique stars and 501 high-resolution
  echelle exposures in V3.0-V3.3 with Keplerian planetary de-Doppler and 2D CCD/Hawaii-2RG
  vetoes), narrowband radio technosignatures (multi-epoch exoplanet-drift de-Doppler
  with ON/OFF controls), and fast photometric glints (TESS pixel-covariance qualification).
authors:
  - family-names: "Andersen"
    given-names: "Martin"
version: 0.8.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
repository-code: "https://github.com/andersenmartin-blip/setisearch"
url: "https://github.com/andersenmartin-blip/setisearch"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - SETI
  - technosignatures
  - optical SETI
  - near-infrared SETI
  - echelle spectroscopy
  - HARPS
  - ESPRESSO
  - NIRPS
  - FEROS
  - narrowband radio signals
  - exoplanets
  - reproducible research
